          "text": "I can't give you a schedule that keeps Tuesdays and Thursdays free. I ran the builder twice, and both times it returned schedules with classes on those days. I'm not going to present them as meeting your request.\n\nThese sections meet on Tuesday and/or Thursday:\n- CSE 212-02, 12:45\u20131:45 T/R\n- WDD 231-01, 11:30\u201312:30 T/R\n- REL 275-01, 10:15\u201311:15 T/R\n- REL 275-02, 12:45\u20131:45 T/R\n- MATH 113-03, 11:30\u201312:45 T/R\n- CSE 310-03, M/T/W/R (second block)\n\nThese sections do avoid Tuesday and Thursday. Seats are as of 2026-11-13 15:00 UTC:\n- CSE 310-02 (Applied Programming, 3 cr), M/W/F 12:45\u20131:45, 5 open seats\n- MATH 113-02 (Calculus II, 3 cr), M/W/F 10:15\u201311:15, 3 open seats\n- CIT 225-01 (Database Design, 3 cr), M/W/F 11:30\u201312:30, 6 open seats\n- MATH 221A-01 (Business Statistics, 3 cr), M/W/F 12:45\u20131:45, 9 open seats. It conflicts with CSE 310-02, so you can take only one of them at those times.\n- CSE 212-03 (Data Structures, 2 cr), online with no set meeting times, 15 open seats\n- CSE 212-04 (Data Structures, 2 cr), M/W 3:15\u20134:15, second block, 9 open seats\n\nFor WDD 231 and REL 275, the only sections I found meet on Tuesday and Thursday. I haven't checked CSE 270, CSE 340/341 or the elective options yet.\n\nWould you like me to search those courses for sections that fit your Tuesday and Thursday days off? Or should I build a schedule without WDD 231 and REL 275 for now?\n\nConfirm with BYU-Idaho Academic Advising.",
